  "articleBody": "Trip hazards are a major concern, especially if you or a loved one uses a walker. The good news is, many of them are easy to fix! First, tackle those pesky throw rugs. If they're not absolutely necessary, consider removing them. If you keep them, make sure they have a non-slip backing and aren't curled up at the edges. Next, take a good look at your pathways. Is there furniture blocking a clear route from the bedroom to the bathroom, or from the living room to the kitchen? Rearranging a few pieces can open up a lot of space. Clutter can also be a hidden tripping hazard – those stacks of magazines or extra boxes need to find a new home. Even simple things like ensuring cords are neatly tucked away and not across walkways makes a difference. For more persistent issues, like uneven floor transitions or thresholds that are hard to navigate, professional help from HH Remodeling LLC might be just what you need. We can help you identify and eliminate these hazards to make your home safer. Call us at 303-505-0866 to discuss how we can help.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}